      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on the wiki, here\u0027s how the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment:\n\n**The Hub uses credential scoping** \u2014 it never holds the API key in its own process environment at all. Instead:\n\n1. **At startup**, a local secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file\n2. **Before spawning a child process**, the key is injected directly into only that child process\u0027s environment\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 the credential never exists there\n\nThis architecture means that even if the Hub process were compromised or misbehaving, it cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables. The key only exists inside the short-lived child process that actually makes the API calls.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to both the Ingest agent and the Query agent \u2014 each receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from the Hub.\n\nSee [[credential-scoping]] for the full details.",
